    ; ── binding patterns (parser slice 10) ──────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; parseIdentifierOrPattern and the four routines under it. Three call sites
    ; reach them — a variable declaration (the catch clause's binding included,
    ; which routes through the same one), a parameter's name, and
    ; skip_parameter_start's look-ahead — and they are the same three the
    ; reference has.
    ;
    ; ★ The reference threads a DIAGNOSTIC MESSAGE through here
    ; (parseIdentifierOrPatternWithDiagnostic), and its two callers pass
    ; different ones: "private identifiers are not allowed in variable
    ; declarations" (18029) and "private identifiers cannot be used as
    ; parameters" (18009). It was left out through slice 12 with the §3.5q
    ; argument written down — the only thing it could change was WHICH
    ; diagnostic a private identifier gets, and a private identifier was refused
    ; one level down as unported either way. That is a §3.5p claim, and slice
    ; 13c is its expiry: the two codes are now the whole difference between
    ; `var #x` and `function f(#x)`.
    procedure parse_identifier_or_pattern(mutable this) @page true @returnpage true @deep true returns ref[AstNode]? linked


