    ; ── the JSX grammar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; Slice 20. Sixteen parse routines and three scanner drivers, and the shape
    ; to hold on to is that LAST part: this grammar is the one place where the
    ; parser tokenizes. Every routine that finishes a tag ends by choosing
    ; between `next_token()` and `scan_jsx_text()` — the same source position,
    ; two different tokenizations — because whether what follows is document text
    ; or an expression is a question only the parser can answer. So the ordinary
    ; scan loop is bypassed here, and the token yardstick, which calls scan() in a
    ; loop, cannot see any of this. The parse yardstick is the only witness.

