    ; ── lists, and the RECOVERY that makes them lists ───────────────────────
    ;
    ; parseList / parseDelimitedList / parseBracketedList, with the error
    ; recovery slice 13c added. Through slice 12 the recovery was the one thing
    ; deliberately left out, on the argument that "recovery only runs after a
    ; diagnostic, and a diagnostic is already an unported report" — which was
    ; true and which this slice retires along with the premise.
    ;
    ; A list may legitimately come back EMPTY — `Foo<>` is a type reference with
    ; zero type arguments, and the reference builds an empty NodeList for it —
    ; so an empty Array here is a result, not a failure. Failure is null, and
    ; null now means only one thing: an element parser met a construct this port
    ; does not implement and said so.

    ; ★ createMissingList — the reference's answer when the OPENING token was
    ; absent. It is an empty list carrying a marker (`missingListNodes`) that
    ; later passes read; ForEachChild visits a list's ELEMENTS, of which there
    ; are none, so for this yardstick the marker is invisible and an empty list
    ; is the whole of it.
