    procedure skip_parameter_start(mutable this) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool linked





















    ; skipParameterStart's binding-pattern arm: "return true if we can parse an
    ; array or object binding pattern with no errors", which the reference asks
    ; as `previousErrorCount == len(p.diagnostics)` across the parse. This port's
    ; stand-in for that list is the `unported` record — §3.5i gives it the
    ; reference's LIFETIME for exactly this reason — so the port is the same
    ; before/after comparison over the records we keep.
    ;
    ; ★★★ But the two are not the same PREDICATE, and that is why a recorded
    ; report answers `unanswerable` here rather than `false`. Our record fires
    ; for two reasons: a construct the reference DIAGNOSES, where `false` is
    ; right, and one it parses perfectly well that this port has not built, where
    ; `false` is a quiet wrong answer — it would route `([a]: T) => U` down the
    ; parenthesized-type path and build a tree nobody has checked. Nothing at
    ; this site can tell the two apart, so it reports; over-reporting is the
    ; direction this harness exists to err in. §3.9e.
    ;
    ; ★ This is still the ONE site whose report must outlive a rewind, which is
    ; the whole reason there are two records: every caller is a look-ahead, so a
    ; rewindable report would be erased the moment the ANSWER was handed back and
    ; used. What slice 10 changes is how OFTEN it fires — a clean pattern now
    ; answers `true`, and only a pattern that hits something unported reports.
    ;
    ; ★ Both records are compared, not just `unported`: the recursion can reach
    ; this very function again (`{ a = ([b]: T) => c }`), and a nested
    ; `unanswerable` is a report about this parse too.
    ; ★★★ Slice 13c makes the reference's own test AVAILABLE — it counts its
    ; diagnostics before and after — and that does NOT retire the two records
    ; above it, which is the half worth reading. §3.5w says a port's stand-in can
    ; match a mechanism's lifetime and still not match its MEANING: a construct
    ; this port has not built leaves no diagnostic at all, so the count would
    ; answer "clean" for a parse that never happened. The count is therefore the
    ; LAST test here, not the only one.
    procedure skip_binding_pattern(mutable this) @ret_param_0 true @deep true returns bool linked












    ; ... and the same again for the record a rewind does not restore.
    procedure unanswerable_bool(mutable this, tag: Slice[char]) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true @deep_this_2 true @deep_whole_2 true returns bool linked










